The schedule for the 2008 SELinux Developer Summit has been published at:

    http://selinuxproject.org/page/Developer_Summit_2008/Schedule

To emphasize collaboration and allow great coverage of topics, the format of
the summit is to be a series of discussion panels with brief presentations.

Panel sessions are as follows:

    o Community
    o Applications
    o Desktop
    o Distributed Technologies
    o Policy Configuration
    o Policy Infrastructure
    o Emerging Technology/Works in Progress

Detailed information on topics and issues to be discussed may be found
at the URL listed above.

All SELinux developers and others with a technical interest in the project
are encouraged to attend.  (Please note again that attendees must also be
registered to attend OLS).

Please direct any discussion of the summit to the main SELinux mailing list,
or to the organizing team: selinux-summit-team AT namei.org.


